t State\\n\\n- **Revision**: `2dc177328588108815b51f713032270315e8419d`\\n- **Working tree**: clean (nothing to commit)\\n- **Prior results file**: `reports/real-world-results.json` (4 entries)\\n- **Output artifact**: not generated (run did not start)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Next Concrete Fix\\n\\nThe workflow (`weekly-real-world-testing.md`) configures `dollarlint-repo` as a Docker-sidecar MCP server (`container: golang:1.26.3`). To fix this:\\n\\n1. **Verify Docker-in-Docker support** in the GitHub Actions runner for agentic workflows (`gh-aw`), or\\n2. **Re-configure** the `dollarlint-repo` MCP server to run as a native host process (not in a container), or\\n3. **Expand the bash allowlist** in `weekly-real-world-testing.md` to include `git clone`, `go build`, and `dollarlint` so the agent can manually run the corpus pipeline without the MCP server.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Raw diagnostics</summary>\\n\\n- `cat /proc/net/tcp`: Port 8080 (0x1F90) not found in listening state\\n- `cat /home/runner/work/_temp/gh-aw/mcp-cli/manifest.json`: dollarlint-repo server listed at `http://host.docker.internal:8080/mcp/dollarlint-repo`\\n- MCP CLI bridge binary exists but requires `node` to invoke (blocked)\\n- `/opt/hostedtoolcache/go/1.26.3/x64/bin/go` exists but `go version` is blocked by policy\\n- Workflow run: https://github.com/dollarlint/dollarlint/actions/runs/25609301820\\n\\n</details>\\n\", \"category\": \"General\"}"
